 # Drone MVP Medium Bag Outer Package Decision
 
-> [!important] Current status (2026-10-19)
-> Rob Knudson's [Weight and Dimension Eligibility PRD](https://wonder.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f40ba91c0864455e9792d8f51b9f008d/pages/5462392836/PRD+Weight+and+Dimension+Eligibility+for+1P+Drone+Delivery), version 26, reports that the **new Medium Wonder bag, 12 × 8.5 × 13 in**, has been validated by Zipline across multiple Wonder packaging configurations and is the default bag for MVP launch SOPs. Small is an IKC-staff operational fallback only; Large is out of scope. This supersedes the September 20 candidate-testing status. The source is Rob's PRD; a separate Zipline test report was not inspected in this update.
+> [!important] Current status (2026-10-28)
+> Rob Knudson's follow-up, relayed by Jay on 2026-10-28, says IKC Ops has **completed the sample testing**: the Medium bag and the guest-packaging samples fit the production Pod, the **Medium bag is confirmed as the MVP outer package**, and **no further bag testing is planned before launch**. This closes the sample-fit test that the 2026-08-12 Slack thread left open. The follow-up does not publish a fill line, folded height, orientation, handle/closure rule, SKU, or tare, and it does not change the Zipline provider envelope. Source: [[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/Slack Clarification - Drone MVP Medium Bag Selection - 2026-08-12|Slack Clarification note, Update (2026-10-28)]].
+
+> [!info] Previous status (2026-10-19)
+> Rob Knudson's [Weight and Dimension Eligibility PRD](https://wonder.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020f40ba91c0864455e9792d8f51b9f008d/pages/5462392836/PRD+Weight+and+Dimension+Eligibility+for+1P+Drone+Delivery), version 26, reports that the **new Medium Wonder bag, 12 × 8.5 × 13 in**, has been validated by Zipline across multiple Wonder packaging configurations and is the default bag for MVP launch SOPs. Small is an IKC-staff operational fallback only; Large is out of scope. This superseded the September 20 candidate-testing status. The source is Rob's PRD; a separate Zipline test report was not inspected in that update.
 
 ## Short Answer
 
-The MVP default is the **new Medium Wonder bag, 12 × 8.5 × 13 in**, per PRD v26. Small may be used at IKC staff discretion when a specific order can safely be packed smaller; Large must not be used for Drone delivery.
+The MVP outer package is the **Medium Wonder bag**: PRD v26 (2026-10-19) names the new Medium, 12 × 8.5 × 13 in, as the default, and the 2026-10-28 follow-up confirms IKC Ops sample testing is complete, with the Medium bag and guest-packaging samples fitting the production Pod and no further bag testing planned before launch. Small may be used at IKC staff discretion when a specific order can safely be packed smaller; Large must not be used for Drone delivery.
 
 Validation of the bag does not approve every cart. The PRD still requires item-level weight and dimensions to be submitted to Zipline Pack for order-specific evaluation. It does not specify the bag SKU, tare, tested fill/fold limits, or partner-site configuration. KDS/KOM remains an operational instruction surface rather than the physical fit authority.
 
